dash='## Quant & Market Dashboard\n\n### Liquidity and volatility\n\n- **Overnight:** Index futures are higher at the story’s 05:39 CST checkpoint. ES/NQ spreads, depth, overnight volume, ETF executable quotes and Treasury-market depth are unverified; price direction is not a liquidity measure. Refresh the execution feed before the cash auction.\n- **Funding:** Latest verified SOFR is 3.92% for November 5, published November 6 at 07:02 CST. Today’s fixing was not yet available at cutoff. Lagged funding is not a current stress diagnosis. [FRED SOFR](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/SOFR).\n- **Regime: Moderate, with elevated transition risk; medium confidence.** Delayed VIX was 23.31 at November 9 06:39 EST / 05:39 CST, versus Friday’s daily-row close of 25.64. House thresholds: below 15 low, 15–25 moderate, 25–35 high, above 35 stressed; not calibrated forecasts. Current skew, term structure and dealer gamma remain unverified. [VIX](https://chartexchange.com/symbol/index-vix/historical/).\n\n### Factor proxies\n\n| Factor | ETF | Nov 5→6 | Oct 9→Nov 6 (4 weeks) |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Momentum | [MTUM](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/mtum/history/) | +1.85% | -20.30% |\n| Value | [VLUE](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/vlue/history/) | +0.11% | -8.69% |\n| Quality | [QUAL](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/qual/history/) | +0.07% | -3.43% |\n| Size | [IWM](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/iwm/history/) | +0.99% | -1.89% |\n| Growth | [IWF](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/iwf/history/) | +1.26% | -12.63% |\n| Low volatility | [SPLV](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/splv/history/) | -0.93% | +6.56% |\n\nPrice returns from the source-linked Close columns, excluding distributions; these are ETF proxies, not isolated factor premia. October 9 comparison inputs are archived from November 7; November 6 closes were rechecked November 9; no new completed cash session exists. Corporate-action histories were not independently refreshed; keep a common adjustment basis. Momentum and growth rebounded on Friday but remain sharply negative over four weeks; low volatility fell Friday but remains positive over that horizon.\n\n### Execution and microstructure\n\n- For today, Monday November 9, cash opening auction is 8:30 a.m. CST / 14:30 UTC. Recheck the economic calendar before staging orders; CPI is Tuesday at 7:30 a.m. CST; results unknown at cutoff. [BLS calendar](https://www.bls.gov/schedule/2026/11_sched_list.htm).\n- Inspect quote age, NBBO spreads, displayed depth, auction imbalances and ES/NQ basis. Use bounded limits and participation caps; stress gaps, cancellations, missed fills, latency and widened spreads. Rising prices on thin depth can trap liquidity takers.\n- Options: refresh post-expiry positions and hedge requirements; verify expiry, deliverables and settlement. Reject stale, crossed or one-sided quotes. Dealer-gamma sign, expiry concentrations and pinning remain unknown.\n\n**Research watchlist:** SPY, QQQ, IWM, RSP, TLT; ES, NQ, ZN, VX; MTUM, VLUE, QUAL, IWF, SPLV; NVDA, KKR.\n\n### DRL Improvements for the MATLAB System\n\n1. Keep drawdown, exposure, participation and stale-data limits outside the policy, with a safe fallback.\n2. Penalize spread, impact, turnover, latency and missed fills; evaluate tail losses separately from reward.\n3. Keep future-return targets in training folds only; purge overlapping horizons and reserve a one-use final holdout.\n4. Randomize liquidity and observation delays across regimes; test whether abstention preserves risk compliance under distribution shift.\n\n### Model hygiene\n\nAudit leakage, survivorship bias, look-ahead, corporate actions, stale options quotes, multiple testing, calibration and drift. Use point-in-time universes, release vintages and availability timestamps. Fit preprocessing on training folds only; keep memory curation separate from point-in-time numerical evaluation.\n\n### MATLAB optimization patterns\n\n- Use named-zone timetables and causal synchronize/retime; never backfill unreleased observations.\n- Vectorize rolling features, preallocate logs and profile before optimizing.\n- Parallelize independent folds or Bayesian trials with reproducible random streams and fixed budgets.\n- Use GPUs for suitable batches; keep data, risk controls and evaluation in modular environments.\n\n### High-value quant research question\n\n**Does an explicit abstention gate based on spread, depth and quote age improve net out-of-sample results during volatility-regime transitions?**\n\nCompare identical policies with and without the gate, matching seeds, action budgets and costs. Test missed opportunity alongside drawdown and slippage; it distinguishes useful restraint from accidental underexposure.\n'
